 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nobject_len function fails to handle basic collection types\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `object_len` function in `astroid/helpers.py` is not properly handling basic Python collection types like lists, tuples, dictionaries, and sets. When trying to infer the length of these collections, the function fails to return the expected length values.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport astroid\n\n# Test with list\nnode = astroid.extract_node(\"len(['a','b','c'])\")\nresult = next(node.infer())\nprint(f\"Expected: 3, Got: {result.as_string()}\")\n\n# Test with dict\nnode = astroid.extract_node(\"a = {'a': 1, 'b': 2}\\nlen(a)\")\nresult = next(node.infer())\nprint(f\"Expected: 2, Got: {result.as_string()}\")\n\n# Test with variable containing list\nnode = astroid.extract_node(\"a = [1,2,'a','b','c']\\nlen(a)\")\nresult = next(node.infer())\nprint(f\"Expected: 5, Got: {result.as_string()}\")\n```\n\nThe above code should return the correct length values but currently fails to do so. This affects various inference operations that depend on length calculations, including more complex scenarios like `random.sample` calls that use `len()` as arguments.\n</issue>\n",
